# $project_name

Generated by `snapadmin-new` (django-snapadmin $snapadmin_version) — a runnable Django +
SnapAdmin project: an admin panel, a REST API (with Swagger docs) and a GraphQL endpoint,
all generated from the models in `$app_name/models.py`.

## Run it

    pip install django-snapadmin
    python manage.py migrate
    python manage.py createsuperuser
    python manage.py runserver

Then open:

- http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/ — the admin panel
- http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/docs/ — Swagger / OpenAPI docs
- http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/graphql/ — GraphiQL (while `DEBUG=True`)

No Docker, no PostgreSQL, no manual settings edits — SQLite is the default database.

## The worked example

`$app_name/models.py` declares one `SnapModel` (`Product`) with a few `Snap*Field`s. Each
one drives the generated admin, REST API and GraphQL schema automatically — add a field
there and it shows up everywhere with no further wiring. `$app_name/admin.py` registers it
with one call, `SnapModel.register_all_admins()`. See
https://drofji.github.io/django-snapadmin/ for the full field and settings reference.

## Configuration

Environment variables are documented in `dist.env` — copy it to `.env` and adjust; the
project also runs correctly with no `.env` at all (every setting has a sensible default).
